---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Editorial Policy | MotorByte"
  description="MotorByte's editorial standards for accuracy, corrections, opinion, and clearly disclosed commercial relationships."
>
  <article class="mx-auto max-w-3xl px-5 py-16 sm:px-8 sm:py-20">
    <p class="text-xs font-bold uppercase tracking-[0.2em] text-orange-400">How we publish</p>
    <h1 class="mt-4 text-4xl font-black tracking-tight text-white sm:text-5xl">Editorial policy</h1>
    <div class="prose-post mt-8">
      <p>MotorByte aims to publish clear, accurate, and original automotive writing. Articles should offer readers context or a useful perspective, not simply repeat headlines or repackage other publishers’ work.</p>
      <h2>Accuracy and corrections</h2>
      <p>We aim to verify factual claims with reliable sources and distinguish confirmed information from speculation. If we find a material error, we will correct it and update the article where appropriate. Readers can send correction requests through our <a href="/contact/">contact page</a>.</p>
      <h2>Opinion and commercial relationships</h2>
      <p>Opinion pieces represent the author’s views. Sponsored articles, paid placements, gifted products, affiliate links, or other material relationships must be clearly disclosed to readers. Editorial coverage is not an endorsement by a vehicle manufacturer.</p>
      <h2>Authorship</h2>
      <p>Articles identify their author. Contributors should only be credited for work they actually wrote or materially contributed to.</p>
    </div>
  </article>
</BaseLayout>
